            "review_text": "Lewis\nHanoi, Vietnam3 contributions\n0\nWould not come here again!\nMar 2023 • Couples\nDelicious food but very terrible staff experience. Please read this fully and carefully - it’s long but it’s necessary.\n\nWe came here for lunch time and was the second to arrive after a 2-person table. After us there were around 3-4 other tables. We waited from around 11h20 to 11h40 and still hadn’t got anything placed on our table (not even a simple bottle of water and ice tea that I ordered). And somehow I saw another table coming AFTER us got the food served first. Not just one, but two dishes. That was when we got really confused and decided to ask a tall bold American - European guy wearing staff uniform where were our food? And was met by a very, VERY RUDE attitude. \n\nI tried to explain to him that how we got here first and how long we were waiting and how another table got served first, but somehow it seemed that this guy did not understand me at all. When I said: “we were the first to arrive”, he immediately snapped at me: “no they (he meant the table got the food) were here first.” The conversation went back and forth like some kind of a kindergarten fight when I kept saying “no we were” and he said “no you weren’t”. I found this ridiculous. I could not made this up - there were literally surveillance cameras over the section we were sitting. When I tried to say more, he cut me off (a very childish behavior again) and signaled that he did not want any of this nonsense conversation anymore. The staff who took our order was a different lady, so I tried to tell him to check with her because she knew we arrive first. He said something along the line of “no i am the boss here and you tell me, you don’t need to tell her.” And “the food will get here when it gets here.”\n\nWow. Normally when you had a bad experience at a restaurant you would like to report to the manager. But I didn’t know what to do when the one’s at fault here is the manager himself 😅 huge disrespect to the customer, not even wanting to solve the problem. Eventually our food arrived but he put our dish on the table like it was some kind of disgusting disease that he never wanted to touch - I bet he did that and walked away in 2 seconds. Feels like the food was thrown out to us rather than served.\n\nI understand that sometime mistakes are not unavoidable, and you might have a bad day, but that was no excuse to treat your customers like this. I am happy and willing to wait for our food if only he had not cut me off like that. It took everything not to walk away of the restaurant and left (cause even though I was mad our food order has already been taken care of). And again 😂 this is the MANAGER ACTING RUDE HIMSELF. Who can I report to but to leave a one star review here.\n\nCustomers are not God, but we have the right to expect the services the same quality that we paid for (the food here was average not cheap). And I will not edit this post because every little details I said it’s true, I can even provide the time and date needed to check.\n\nI highly suggests a change of staff and a training courses for them. The only reason this reviews stays at 1 star because it is the lowest I can rate, and because the food were indeed nice.\nRead more\nWritten March 5, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
